<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalmar Nyckel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1638</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar">Kalmar</a> Nyckel was a Dutch-built armed merchant ship that carried the first Swedish colonists to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. Sailing with the smaller Fogel Grip under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-minuit">Peter Minuit</a>, it reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delaware-river">Delaware River</a> in March 1638, where the settlers founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-christina">Fort Christina</a>, the beginning of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. It made four round trips across the Atlantic for the colony, and a full-scale replica was launched in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilmington-delaware">Wilmington, Delaware</a>, in 1997.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalmar-nyckel.jpg" alt="Kalmar Nyckel" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob Hägg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalmar_Nyckel_by_Jacob_H%C3%A4gg_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
